{
 "contract": "uct.converse-eval.cases/1",
 "_": "ONE RUNNING VALUE at the door, as cases (Studio, 2026-11-18). A capability census found twelve indicator ideas the ENGINE computes and the door refused, each a value that reads its own previous value: `accum(seed, update, warmup)` with `self`. The door now lets the assistant write ONE such value. Examples: a streak (a count), a stop that only rises (a level), a fixed-gain smoother (the one shape that provably settles), Kaufman's adaptive average and the McGinley Dynamic. Each scripted answer is the formula; the case holds that the door accepts it in one call, the browser's own patch engine applies it, and the engine computes it. `ctl-two-running-values` is the NEW negative control: two values that feed each other (`accum2`, `state1`) stay closed and are refused by name. The standard controls ride along. Kaufman's adaptive average and the McGinley Dynamic are NAMES in the named-indicator library (api/data/named_indicators.json), so their scripted answers are the library's own formulas.",
 "chart": {
  "sym": "TEST",
  "tf": "D"
 },
 "bars": 1500,
 "cases": [
  {
   "id": "run-streak",
   "group": "example",
   "turns": [
    {
     "words": "Count how many days in a row the close has been up, in a lower pane.",
     "expect": {
      "kind": "change",
      "outputs": [
       {
        "type": "series",
        "tree": {
         "type": "call",
         "name": "accum",
         "args": [
          {
           "type": "num",
           "value": 0
          },
          {
           "type": "op",
           "name": "?:",
           "args": [
            {
             "type": "op",
             "name": ">",
             "args": [
              {
               "type": "series",
               "name": "close"
              },
              {
               "type": "offset",
               "value": 1,
               "args": [
                {
                 "type": "series",
                 "name": "close"
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "op",
             "name": "+",
             "args": [
              {
               "type": "series",
               "name": "self"
              },
              {
               "type": "num",
               "value": 1
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "type": "num",
             "value": 0
            }
           ]
          },
          {
           "type": "num",
           "value": 100
          }
         ]
        }
       }
      ],
      "max_model_calls": 1
     }
    }
   ]
  },
